Material: {"source_context":[{"end":2244,"id":"S000","reason":"existing-evidence","roles":["scope_text:0"],"start":2025,"text":"(iii) Notwithstanding any other requirement of this chapter, occupy an approved child restraint system furnished by the operator or one of the persons described in paragraph (a)(3)(iii)(A) of this section provided that:"},{"end":4357,"id":"S001","reason":"focus-or-structural-adjacent","start":4019,"text":"( 4 ) Except as provided in § 91.107(a)(3)(iii)(B)( 3 )( iii ) and § 91.107(a)(3)(iii)(B)( 3 )( iv ), booster-type child restraint systems (as defined in Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard No. 213 (49 CFR 571.213)), vest- and harness-type child restraint systems, and lap held child restraints are not approved for use in aircraft; and"},{"end":4417,"id":"S002","reason":"focus-or-structural-adjacent","roles":["scope_text:1"],"start":4359,"text":"(C) The operator complies with the following requirements:"},{"end":4515,"id":"S003","reason":"existing-evidence","roles":["summary"],"start":4359,"text":"(C) The operator complies with the following requirements:\n\n( 1 ) The restraint system must be properly secured to an approved forward-facing seat or berth;"},{"end":4375,"id":"S004","reason":"existing-evidence","roles":["actor"],"start":4363,"text":"The operator"},{"end":4515,"id":"S005","reason":"focus-or-structural-adjacent","roles":["scope_text:2"],"start":4419,"text":"( 1 ) The restraint system must be properly secured to an approved forward-facing seat or berth;"},{"end":4450,"id":"S006","reason":"existing-evidence","roles":["modality"],"start":4446,"text":"must"},{"end":4658,"id":"S007","reason":"focus-or-structural-adjacent","start":4517,"text":"( 2 ) The child must be properly secured in the restraint system and must not exceed the specified weight limit for the restraint system; and"}],"statement":"When a child occupies an approved child restraint system under 14 CFR § 91.107(a)(3)(iii), the operator must ensure the restraint system 